+    "honest_scope_statement": "AT THE SHIPPED BUDGET THIS IS A SINGLE-GAME, SINGLE-OBSERVATION RESULT, NOT A CORPUS ESTIMATE. Of 75 control cells 64 reach ZERO levels and only 3 reach two -- and all of those are the same game (vc33), so every level-regression at b400 is one game's. The largest at-risk gap that sets the safe-window boundary comes from ONE seed of that game. With at most 2 at-risk cells the smallest two-sided p reachable is 0.5, so NO significance on the regression question is attainable at b400 no matter how many seeds are added to these games. Separately, 91.35% of the corpus score total sits in 4 of 75 cells (the top cell alone 52.58%), so a reported score delta is a statement about those cells, not a corpus effect. For a safety claim intended to generalise, read the b4000 condition, whose movable set is an order of magnitude larger -- and note its `score_sums_are_corpus_level: false`."
